and creating magnesium oxide.

00:02:09.962 --> 00:02:11.964
And that's what the smoke is.
-Oh, my gosh.

00:02:11.964 --> 00:02:14.767
-So it burns more energetically.
It's kind of more unique.

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:16.935
-Now, are we allowed to breathe
in magnesium oxide?

00:02:16.935 --> 00:02:19.205
-Uh...we're fine.
-Okay, alright.

00:02:19.205 --> 00:02:21.474
Thank you, Kevin.
-It's a big room.

00:02:21.474 --> 00:02:23.810
There's not too much of it.
-Oh, my gosh. This is awesome.

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:25.744
Alright, I got to do that, yeah.
-Pretty good.

00:02:25.744 --> 00:02:28.982
-Yeah. So, kids, ask Santa for
shaved magnesium for Christmas.

00:02:28.982 --> 00:02:31.284
-Yeah. Exactly.
-What do we got next, bud?

00:02:31.284 --> 00:02:34.654
-So now we have a snowball
kind of bowling ball.

00:02:34.654 --> 00:02:37.022
So, what we're going to
talk about now is

00:02:37.022 --> 00:02:39.225
the law of
conservation of energy.

00:02:39.225 --> 00:02:41.460
So, energy can't be
created or destroyed.

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:43.462
It can only convert from
one form to another.

00:02:43.462 --> 00:02:44.631
So that's what we're going to do
with the bowling ball.

00:02:44.631 --> 00:02:46.031
-Okay.

00:02:46.031 --> 00:02:51.237
-So, go ahead and stand up
against that wall over there.

00:02:51.237 --> 00:02:52.771
It's okay. Please, please.

00:02:52.771 --> 00:02:54.640
I'm sorry. That was rude.

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:57.443
-No, that's not why
I was concerned.

00:02:57.443 --> 00:02:59.179
-So, okay...
-Oh, my gosh.

00:02:59.179 --> 00:03:00.880
-...take this bowling ball...
-Okay.

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:02.248
-...and hold it up to your nose.

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:03.816
I'll hang on to it for now.
-Thank you. Yeah.

00:03:03.816 --> 00:03:06.285
-So, right now,
what we have here is --

00:03:06.285 --> 00:03:07.520
we have potential energy.

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:08.955
When you let go of the ball,

00:03:08.955 --> 00:03:11.490
it's going to move that way
and convert to kinetic energy.

00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:13.593
It's going to reach its maximum
around the bottom there,

00:03:13.593 --> 00:03:16.128
when it --
you know, at the base,

00:03:16.128 --> 00:03:17.564
when it's low, I guess.

00:03:17.564 --> 00:03:21.033
And then it's going to keep
swinging and convert back into

00:03:21.033 --> 00:03:22.935
potential energy
and then swing back.

00:03:22.935 --> 00:03:25.238
Now, because we're not going to
give it any force,

00:03:25.238 --> 00:03:30.076
it's not going to go
farther back this way

00:03:30.076 --> 00:03:32.111
than you released it, okay?

00:03:32.111 --> 00:03:34.747
It's not going to go past
your face,

00:03:34.747 --> 00:03:36.215
unless you give it extra force.

00:03:36.215 --> 00:03:39.719
-Well, then how come you're not
standing here if it's so...

00:03:39.719 --> 00:03:40.886
-You can stand -- It's fine.

00:03:40.886 --> 00:03:42.087
So, you want to hold it up
to your nose.

00:03:42.087 --> 00:03:44.257
Now you want to just
let go, okay?

00:03:44.257 --> 00:03:46.192
And you don't give it
any force at all.

00:03:46.192 --> 00:03:48.027
-Alright. Just let go
and don't give it any force.

00:03:48.027 --> 00:03:49.361
And stand here?
-Yeah.

00:03:49.361 --> 00:03:50.830
-And what if I get hit in
the face with a bowling ball?

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:54.033
-You probably won't.
[ Drumroll ]

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:55.334
Okay, ready?
-I think so.

00:03:55.334 --> 00:03:58.972
-3, 2, 1...
